PRACTICAL 6 — PHP WITH MONGODB

STEP 1: COPY PHP MONGODB EXTENSION

Copy:
php_mongo.dll

Paste it into:
C:\xampp\php\ext\


STEP 2: EDIT PHP CONFIGURATION

Open:
C:\xampp\php\php.ini

Find the extensions section.

Add:
extension=php_mongo.dll

Save the file.


STEP 3: LAUNCH MONGO SHELL

Open MongoDB Shell.


STEP 4: CREATE PHP FILES

Create:

insert.php
update.php
retrieve.php

Save all files in:

C:\xampp\htdocs\

While saving, select:

Save as type: All Files


STEP 5: START XAMPP

Open XAMPP.

Start:
Apache

Click:
Admin

Browser opens:
http://localhost/dashboard

Replace dashboard with the PHP filename.

Example:
http://localhost/insert.php


1. INSERT — insert.php

<?php

$m = new MongoClient();

echo "Connection to database successfully";

$db = $m -> MYDB269758;

echo "\nCollection selected successfully";

$col = $db -> MyCol;

echo "\nCollection selected successfully";

$doc = array(
    "name" => "Ashwini",
    "age" => 20,
    "dept" => "TYIT",
    "rollno" => 269758
);

$col -> insert($doc);

echo "\nDocument inserted successfully";

?>


RUN:

http://localhost/insert.php


2. UPDATE — update.php

<?php

$m = new MongoClient();

echo "Connection to database successfully";

$db = $m -> MYDB269758;

echo "\nCollection selected successfully";

$col = $db -> MyCol;

echo "\nCollection selected successfully";

$col -> update(array("name" => "Ashwini"),array('$set'=>array("age" => 19)));

echo "\nDocument updated successfully";

?>


RUN:

http://localhost/update.php


3. RETRIEVE — retrieve.php

<?php

$m = new MongoClient();

echo "\nConnection database successfully";

$db = $m -> MYDB269758;

echo "\nDatabase selected successfully";

$col = $db -> MyCol;

echo "\nCollection selected successfully";

$cursor = $col -> find();

foreach($cursor as $doc)
{
    echo "<br/>";
    echo $doc["name"]."<br/>";
    echo $doc["age"]."<br/>";
    echo $doc["dept"]."<br/>";
    echo $doc["rollno"]."<br/>";
}

?>


RUN:
http://localhost/retrieve.php

4.DELETE - delete.php

<?php

$m = new MongoClient();

echo "Connection to database successfully";

$db = $m->MYDB239720;

echo "\nDatabase selected successfully";

$col = $db->MyCol;

echo "\nCollection selected successfully";

$col->remove(array("name" => "Romal"));

echo "\nDocument deleted successfully";

?>


RUN:
http://localhost/delete.php

